{
  "comment": [
    "Shared host classification vectors for a plain-HTTP Metro server URL.",
    "class: what every classifier returns for this exact host string: metro-url-policy (Rust), classifyHost",
    "(apps/desktop/src/api/serverUrl.ts) and hostClass (crates/server/src/admin_web/admin.js).",
    "installer: what the runner installers (install-metro-runner-linux.sh, metro-runner-container.sh and",
    "metro-runner-container.ps1) do with http://<host>:8787 when it differs from class. They take only the exact",
    "loopback literals localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1], and refuse other names for this machine, trailing dots and",
    "malformed hosts. A trailing dot sends the name through the resolver, so 100.64.0.1. and localhost. are other."
